The five Bundesrat endpoints below have only the placeholder files <endpoint>.yaml today (see the card about the .yaml placeholders) - the CLI shows their answer as a raw YAML dump. The shapes of the XML answers were measured live on 2026-10-20 with view=renderXml, so the templates are built without an API call.

Measured shapes (parsed with the XML parser of the repo):
- bundesrat_startlist: list.item[] - per row name, date, layoutDate, md5, url
- bundesrat_aktuelles: list.item[] - date, dateOfIssue, title, bodyText, type, id, url, detail, highlighted, imgDates
- bundesrat_termine: list.item[] - title, description, startdate, stopdate, type, id, url, detail
- bundesrat_mitglieder: list.employee[] - name, firstname, honorificTitle, party, state, brmitglied, bv, designiert, mitglied, imagePath, imageDate, detailImgDates, url, detail
- bundesrat_praesidium: list.item[] - title, imageCaption, imagePath, date, dateOfIssue, abstract, detail, id, type

The fields detail and bodyText contain HTML and do not belong in a template.

Templates: one file <endpoint>.yml per endpoint in all seven languages (de, en, fr, es, it, nl, pl), in the style of the existing files (see share/templates/de/autobahn_closures.yml). The headers are translated, the field names stay as the API delivers them.

| endpoint | type | extract | columns |
|---|---|---|---|
| bundesrat_startlist | table | list.item | name, date, url |
| bundesrat_aktuelles | table | list.item | date, title, type, url |
| bundesrat_termine | table | list.item | startdate, title, description |
| bundesrat_mitglieder | table | list.employee | name, firstname, party, state |
| bundesrat_praesidium | table | list.item | title, imageCaption, imagePath, date |

Every template carries a translated empty message that fits the endpoint (German: "Keine Startliste.", "Keine Meldungen.", "Keine Termine.", "Keine Mitglieder.", "Keine Eintraege." - with umlauts, in the language of the file).

Test: t/bundesrat_templates.t (new), offline:
- for every endpoint and every language: the file <endpoint>.yml is there, is readable as YAML, has the type and the extract named above, a non-empty empty message and the column list in the order named above
- a render test: the measured answers of the startlist, the members and the presidency are written into the test as Perl data structures, sent through WWW::Bund::CLI::Formatter with the matching template, and the result is checked - the values show up in the output, no field stays silently empty

The test must be red against the old share/templates (the files are missing there): a behavioural failure, no "Can't locate" error.

